Chapter: CoapParseTest
  cites Encode chapter Coap
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 The round trip is the first assertion: a packet this chapter built is a
 packet this chapter can read back, field for field, including a Block2
 option carrying block 2 / more / szx 6 and a real payload. The builder
 and the parser are written against RFC 7252 separately, so agreeing is
 evidence.

 The refusals are the rest, and they matter more. A parser that cannot
 fail is not a parser -- it is a function that returns something. Each
 case below is a message-format error the RFC names, and each answers
 None rather than a half-filled record: a packet shorter than the header,
 a version of 2, a token length of 9, an option whose value runs past the
 end of the datagram, a payload marker with nothing behind it, and a
 reserved option-delta nibble of 15.

 The empty-payload case is the one to keep. An empty payload is spelled
 by omitting the marker, so a bare 0xFF is a lie about length -- the
 shape of a truncation attack.

Section: Helpers

  bytes-eq : List Integer, List Integer -> Boolean
  bytes-eq (a) (b) =
   if list-length a /= list-length b then False
   else bytes-eq-loop a b 0 (list-length a)

  bytes-eq-loop : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bytes-eq-loop (a) (b) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then True
   else if list-at a i /= list-at b i then False
   else bytes-eq-loop a b (i + 1) len

  flag : Boolean -> Integer
  flag (b) = if b then 1 else 0

  refused : Maybe CoapMessage -> Integer
  refused (m) =
   when m
    is None -> 1
    is Just (x) -> 0

Section: The Round Trip

  sample : List Integer
  sample =
   let opts = [coap-block-option coap-opt-block2 2 1 6]
   in let body = [10, 20, 30, 40]
   in coap-build-request CoapAcknowledgement CoapGet 4660 [171, 205] opts body

  check-round-trip : Integer
  check-round-trip =
   when coap-parse sample
    is None -> 0
    is Just (m) ->
      flag (m.cm-msg-id == 4660)
      + flag (bytes-eq (m.cm-token) [171, 205])
      + flag (bytes-eq (m.cm-payload) [10, 20, 30, 40])
      + flag (list-length (m.cm-options) == 1)

  check-block-decode : Integer
  check-block-decode =
   when coap-parse sample
    is None -> 0
    is Just (m) ->
      when coap-find-option (m.cm-options) coap-opt-block2
       is None -> 0
       is Just (v) ->
         let bv = coap-uint-value v
         in flag (coap-block-num bv == 2)
          + flag (coap-block-more bv == 1)
          + flag (coap-block-szx bv == 6)
          + flag (coap-block-size (coap-block-szx bv) == 1024)

  check-absent-option : Integer
  check-absent-option =
   when coap-parse (coap-build-request CoapConfirmable CoapGet 1 [] [] [7])
    is None -> 0
    is Just (m) ->
      when coap-find-option (m.cm-options) coap-opt-block2
       is None -> 1
       is Just (v) -> 0

 szx 7 is reserved. Answering 2048 for it would walk a caller off the end
 of a buffer, so it answers 0.

  check-reserved-szx : Integer
  check-reserved-szx = flag (coap-block-size 7 == 0)

Section: The Refusals

  check-truncated : Integer
  check-truncated = refused (coap-parse [64, 1])

  check-bad-version : Integer
  check-bad-version = refused (coap-parse [128, 69, 18, 52])

  check-long-token : Integer
  check-long-token = refused (coap-parse [73, 69, 18, 52, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9])

  check-runaway-option : Integer
  check-runaway-option = refused (coap-parse [64, 69, 18, 52, 10, 1, 2])

  check-empty-payload : Integer
  check-empty-payload = refused (coap-parse [64, 69, 18, 52, 255])

  check-reserved-nibble : Integer
  check-reserved-nibble = refused (coap-parse [64, 69, 18, 52, 240, 1])

Section: Body

  opening : Integer =
   check-round-trip
   + check-block-decode
   + check-absent-option
   + check-reserved-szx
   + check-truncated
   + check-bad-version
   + check-long-token
   + check-runaway-option
   + check-empty-payload
   + check-reserved-nibble
